# Pantheon GPU Website Rules

This is the PUBLIC MkDocs Material site for Pantheon (pantheongpu.com):
documentation, mirrored binary releases, and a benchmark leaderboard.
Pantheon source code lives in the private pantheongpu/pantheongpu repo and
must never be committed here.

## Workflow
- Verify before pushing: `python3 -m pytest` and `python3 -m mkdocs build --strict`.
- `docs/assets/web_data.json` is generated from `database/` by
  `python3 website_utils/generate_web_data.py`. Regenerate and commit it after
  changing reports; never hand-edit generated files (including docs/release.md).

## Hard Rules
- Public repo: benchmark reports must not contain host identifiers
  (network_info, hostname, IP address).
- Vendored frontend dependencies only; no CDN scripts.
- All GitHub Actions jobs run on self-hosted Linux runners.
- Use "We" in documentation and outreach copy.
- When fixing a site bug, add a pinning test to tests/test_website_regressions.py.
